00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:33,800
 some separation of those back teeth and these front teeth are banging together and there's

327
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:37,920
 undoubtedly some heavy contact on those incisors.

328
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:43,520
 And secondary occlusal trauma means that there's force on the teeth that usually they could

329
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:50,280
 handle, but in the presence of periodontal attachment loss, it becomes traumatic.

330
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:55,680
 And there's some good evidence for that happening here in this case.

