348
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:34,520
 And lastly, we have peri-implant diseases that go from peri-implant health to peri-implant

349
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:38,160
 mucositis to peri-implantitis.

350
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:44,600
 And risk factors and risk indicators for these disease processes include smoking, diabetes,

351
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:52,240
 poor oral hygiene, poor compliance with supportive care, excess cement, lack of keratinized mucosa

352
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:59,600
 around the implant, and peri-implantitis specifically, a history of previous peri-dontitis around

353
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:00,600
 natural teeth.

354
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:08,520
 There are also some genetic factors that can play a role in this progression.

355
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:14,160
 So peri-implant health involves the absence of visual signs of inflammation and bleeding

356
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:16,360
 on probing.

357
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:21,800
 Implant assessment should consist of visual evaluation, some probing that should be done

358
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:28,280
 at least once per year, evaluation of bleeding on probing of course, and evaluation of radiographic

359
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:36,160
 bone levels compared to a baseline bone level at implant restoration.

360
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:41,960
 It's not really possible to define healthy probing depths around implants, but in general,

361
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:48,080
 peri-implant probing depths should be less than or equal to 5 millimeters.

362
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:53,360
 And this is important that health is possible around implants with normal or reduced bone

363
00:30:53,360 --> 00:30:58,360
 support, just like with healthy gingiva on a reduced peridontium.

364
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:05,200
 As long as you have an absence of progressive bone loss and no signs of inflammation, you

365
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:07,960
 can have peri-implant health.

366
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:16,080
 So this is the equivalent to our peri-dontal health that we saw before.

367
00:31:16,080 --> 00:31:21,200
 Every implant mucusitis involves the presence of visual signs of inflammation and bleeding

368
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,480
 on probing.

369
00:31:22,480 --> 00:31:27,800
 So these signs are things like swelling and redness that you can see here.

370
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:33,240
 Increasing probing depths compared to the baseline and absence of progressive marginal

371
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:35,280
 peri-implant bone loss.

372
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:41,080
 So basically this is like gingivitis, but around an implant.

373
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:46,480
 Ever since that tooth was extracted, this tissue is no longer called gingivia.

374
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,040
 It's called mucosa.

375
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:54,480
 Hence the name peri-implant mucusitis rather than peri-implant gingivitis, but you can

376
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:59,440
 think of it like gingivitis around an implant.

377
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:02,200
 And then the third one was peri-implant titus.

378
00:32:02,200 --> 00:32:06,320
 This involves the presence of visual signs of inflammation and bleeding on probing.

379
00:32:06,320 --> 00:32:12,160
 That's the same, increased probing depths compared to baseline, that's the same, and

380
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:20,040
 this is increased at one year post-implant restoration compared to whatever the baseline

381
00:32:20,040 --> 00:32:22,500
 probing depth was.

382
00:32:22,500 --> 00:32:27,520
 Now in the absence of a baseline recording, we're looking at probing depths that are six

383
00:32:27,520 --> 00:32:33,680
 millimeters or more, and radiographic evidence of three millimeters of bone loss or more.

384
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:40,520
 In peri-implant titus, the big differentiating factor from peri-implant mucusitis is the

385
00:32:40,520 --> 00:32:45,320
 presence of progressive marginal peri-implant bone loss.

386
00:32:45,320 --> 00:32:51,840
 So this is really peri-dontitis around an implant because all these things are similar

387
00:32:51,840 --> 00:32:56,840
 to what we see in a peri-dontitis situation that we're just talking about around implants

388
00:32:56,840 --> 00:33:00,640
 instead of around natural teeth.

389
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,800
 Now putting it all together, I made this summary slide.

390
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:09,680
 The green x's means that you don't have one of these qualities, which is a good thing.

391
00:33:09,680 --> 00:33:15,560
 The red check means that you do have one of these four qualities, which is a bad thing.

392
00:33:15,560 --> 00:33:20,360
 So from health to mucusitis to peri-implant titus.

393
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:27,560
 So the big changes for this 2018 AAP new peri-dontal classification, we have a new classification

394
00:33:27,560 --> 00:33:33,440
 of peri-dontitis, that's this multidimensional staging and greeting that we went over with

395
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:37,120
 the definitions and through four case examples.

396
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:42,960
 We have the consolidation of chronic and aggressive peri-dontitis into a single category.

397
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:48,000
 And we have the addition of these peri-implant diseases and conditions and the clarification

398
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:54,920
 of health and gingivitis on an intact versus a reduced peri-dontum with or without previous

399
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:59,280
 peri-dontitis history.

